SiliconForest QEMU loop: publish /dev/usb_hid_kbd for a generic USB HID keyboard.

On the arm64 `virt` target QEMU's usb-kbd is driven by SFUSBHIDDevice (probe score 6000, above
the boot-keyboard personality whose start() publishes the node). It registers an LED handler,
which runs sf_hid_kbd_setup() and so sets gKbdLock, and from then on SFHIDPushKeyboardEvent()
never calls SFHIDPublishKeyboardDevice(): keys reach the console, but /dev/usb_hid_kbd never
exists (the mouse path publishes on its first event, so /dev/usb_hid_mouse does). Publish
while there is no node, as the mouse path does.

--- a/src/Kernel/Extensions/IOHIDFamily/IOHIDSystem/SFHIDEventQueue.cpp
+++ b/src/Kernel/Extensions/IOHIDFamily/IOHIDSystem/SFHIDEventQueue.cpp
@@ -541,7 +541,7 @@
     UInt32 slot;
     bool kick;
 
-    if (!gKbdLock) SFHIDPublishKeyboardDevice();
+    if (!gKbdLock || !gKbdNode) SFHIDPublishKeyboardDevice();
     if (!sf_hid_kbd_setup()) return;
 
     event.sequence = ++gKbdSequence;
